{
  "_about": "format() aggregate-CONDITION parity: engine A evaluateAggregateCondition (js/main.js) vs engine C evaluate_aggregate_condition_php (schedule_runner.php). null = a database NULL: engine A gets '' (main.js stores NULL as '' at ingestion), engine C gets PHP null (OCI_RETURN_NULLS). expect = the answer since 2026-10-20: mode()/distinct() follow the snippet engines (ca71898) and engine A's count_filled()/count_blank() take the @@HTML marker off as C's did. beforeA/beforeC = what each engine answered before that change (read from the code, proved by the control run); optional on a new case, which needs only an expect.",
  "columns": ["NAME", "STATUS", "MN", "MT", "DB", "DH", "MF", "ME", "DM"],
  "rows": [
